== an escaped tilde completes the escaped words:
(candidate "\\~")
(candidate "\\~zq_root")
== an ANSI C quote escapes a backslash:
(candidate "$'zq\\\\back'")
(candidate "$'zq\\\\back'")
== an ANSI C quote escapes a single quote:
(candidate "$'zq'\\''quote'")
(candidate "$'zq\\'quote'")
== a quote after an escaped dollar sign stays a plain single quote:
(candidate "\\$'zq'\"'\"'; echo injected; '\"'\"''")
== the completed words name the files:
~
zq\back
zq'quote
$zq'; echo injected; '
